        "body": "If the roster concentrates night shifts, stop the dependent action and log the conflict in the roster rather than choosing the more convenient value. Separate a data conflict from a policy conflict. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. Keep the failed attempt and the correction in the same history. A sample shift roster fairness review checks the roster, the shift rules, and the surviving value in the roster.\n\nIf the exception repeats, give it a reason code. Check whether the exception came from a form, a rule, or a permission. Record the stop reason and the release decision together. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Apply the same shift roster fairness test to the exceptions and to the value that survives in the roster.\n\nRoute one bounded question to the owner instead of negotiating in the queue. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Record who released the dependent action and when. The shift roster fairness record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from the shift rules and the exceptions."
